{"id":"f72072773ee22e8e94bfc04166db5cfaab3bde41","axis":"silent","repo":"mlflow/mlflow","sha":"f72072773ee22e8e94bfc04166db5cfaab3bde41","parsed":{"files":[{"path":"docs/docs/self-hosting/workspaces/permissions.mdx","lines":["@@ -16,46 +16,42 @@ A workspace-level grant is a permission on the special"," applies to **every resource type** in that workspace (experiments, registered"," models, prompts, AI Gateway resources). Two levels are grantable:"," ","-- `USE` on `(workspace, *)` is the **Workspace Member** grant. Holders get","-  USE-level access (read + use) to every resource in the workspace, plus","-  the ability to create new experiments and registered models. Per-resource","-  grants can upgrade individual rows. A user _without_ this grant doesn't","-  get a workspace floor; they only get what their specific resource grants","-  provide.","+- `USE` on `(workspace, *)` is the **Workspace Member** grant. Holders can","+  access the workspace and create new experiments and registered models in","+  it. It does not grant read on existing resources; that comes from","+  per-resource or resource-type grants such as `(experiment, *, READ)`. A","+  user _without_ this grant only gets what their resource grants provide."," - `MANAGE` on `(workspace, *)` is the **Workspace Manager** grant. Full","   authority within the workspace, including granting permissions to other","   users via roles in this workspace. Cannot perform system-wide operations","   like deleting users."," ","-A workspace-level grant participates in the same `max` as any per-resource","-grants the user holds, so it acts as a **floor**: per-resource grants can","-upgrade individual rows above the workspace level, but never downgrade them.","-See [Permission resolution](/self-hosting/security/role-based-access-control#permission-resolution)","+A workspace `MANAGE` grant resolves every resource in the workspace to","+`MANAGE`. A workspace `USE` grant does not fold into per-resource checks;","+access to each resource comes from the user's resource grants. See [Permission resolution](/self-hosting/security/role-based-access-control#permission-resolution)"," on the RBAC page for the full mechanic."," "," ### Example scenarios"," ","-1. **Workspace-level grant.** Alice holds the `team-a/user` role, so she has","-   USE-level access (read and use) on every experiment, registered model,","-   and prompt in `team-a`.","-2. **Resource-level upgrade.** Bob holds the `team-a/user` role (`USE`","-   workspace-wide) plus a per-resource grant of `EDIT` on experiment","-   `exp-123`. Bob has USE on every resource in `team-a` and additionally","-   `EDIT` on `exp-123`; the resolver folds matching grants and the","-   higher-priority `EDIT` wins for that resource.","+1. **Workspace Member.** Alice holds the `team-a/user` role. She can see","+   `team-a`, create experiments and registered models there, and read what","+   she creates. To read every experiment, registered model, and prompt in","+   `team-a`, her role also needs `(experiment, *, READ)`,","+   `(registered_model, *, READ)`, and `(prompt, *, READ)`.","+2. **Resource-level grant.** Bob holds the `team-a/user` role plus a","+   per-resource grant of `EDIT` on experiment `exp-123`. Bob can edit","+   `exp-123` and create new resources; other experiments need their own","+   grants."," 3. **Direct resource grant without workspace access.** Carol has `EDIT`","    permission on experiment `exp-456` in `team-a` but no role with","    workspace-level access. Carol can access `exp-456` only, and the","    workspace `team-a` does not appear in her `mlflow.list_workspaces()`","    results."," ","-Because there is no \"explicit deny\" override (see","-[Permission levels](/self-hosting/security/role-based-access-control#permission-levels)),","-a workspace-level grant covers every resource in the workspace and an absent","-(or lesser) per-resource grant cannot revoke it. To restrict access to a","-specific resource, give the user narrower access in the first place:","-per-resource or resource-type-wildcard roles instead of the seeded","-`<workspace>/user` role.","+To let members read every resource of a type, add a resource-type wildcard","+grant such as `(experiment, *, READ)` to their role. To block a specific","+resource, use `DENY` (see","+[Permission levels](/self-hosting/security/role-based-access-control#permission-levels))."," "," ## Default roles"," ","@@ -169,10 +165,9 @@ If users hit permission-denied errors:","        print(r.workspace, r.name)","    ```"," ","-2. Confirm the operation needs more than `USE` (e.g., `EDIT` / `MANAGE`).","-   The resolver folds every matching grant and takes the highest-priority","-   permission level, so a workspace `USE` grant is the floor; if no","-   per-resource grant upgrades it, write operations are denied.","+2. A workspace `USE` grant gives membership and create rights only. Reads","+   and writes on existing resources need a per-resource or resource-type","+   grant (e.g., `READ`, `EDIT`)."," 3. Verify the workspace exists and the role is assigned in the right workspace."," "," ### Workspace not visible in `list_workspaces()`"],"additions":24,"deletions":29,"truncated":false},{"path":"mlflow/server/_request_keys.py","lines":["@@ -8,6 +8,8 @@"," SCOPED_EXPERIMENT_IDS = \"mlflow_scoped_experiment_ids\""," # Flask g key: effective filter retained for scoped-query error reporting."," SCOPED_EXPERIMENT_FILTER = \"mlflow_scoped_experiment_filter\"","+# Flask g key: effective registered model filter retained for scoped-query error reporting.","+SCOPED_REGISTERED_MODEL_FILTER = \"mlflow_scoped_registered_model_filter\""," "," # Starlette request.state keys (FastAPI request scope)"," SCOPED_MCP_SERVER_FILTER = \"mlflow_scoped_mcp_server_filter\""],"additions":2,"deletions":0,"truncated":false},{"path":"mlflow/server/auth/__init__.py","lines":["@@ -282,6 +282,7 @@","     SCOPED_EXPERIMENT_IDS,","     SCOPED_MCP_ACCESS_ENDPOINT_FILTER,","     SCOPED_MCP_SERVER_FILTER,","+    SCOPED_REGISTERED_MODEL_FILTER,"," )"," from mlflow.server.asgi_utils import get_routed_asgi_path"," from mlflow.server.auth.config import DEFAULT_AUTHORIZATION_FUNCTION, read_auth_config","@@ -508,6 +509,7 @@","     SearchExperimentsUtils,","     SearchMCPAccessEndpointUtils,","     SearchMCPServerUtils,","+    SearchModelUtils,"," )"," from mlflow.utils.uri import _decode, get_uri_scheme, is_models_uri, validate_path_is_safe"," from mlflow.utils.validation import (","@@ -3555,21 +3557,11 @@ def _role_based_read_predicate(","     which. A veto is spelled out as ``ACTION_NOT_DENIED`` because that is what the route means;","     a positive action would be honoured too, and reads honestly if a caller ever needs one."," ","-    The row requirement falls back to the workspace tier, which is what the loader this replaced","-    did by folding ``(workspace, \"*\")`` rows in for every resource type. Tier override makes that","-    strictly safer than before: a grant on the row's own key now decides, so","-    ``(experiment, \"*\", DENY)`` is honoured, where previously any workspace-level grant that could","-    read still listed everything.","-","-    NOTE a pre-existing inconsistency this preserves rather than introduces: master folds a","-    workspace grant into a POINT permission only at ``MANAGE``","-    (``get_role_permission_for_resource``, mirrored here by ``is_workspace_admin_grant``), but its","-    predicate loader folded workspace rows in at ANY level. So ``(workspace, \"*\", USE)`` lists","-    experiments it cannot then read. Closing that would deny a caller master allows, so it is left","-    alone and reported as design feedback.","+    The row requirement has no workspace fallback, matching the point routes: a workspace grant","+    reaches a row only at ``MANAGE`` (``is_workspace_admin_grant``, applied by","+    ``retention_gate``), so ``(workspace, \"*\", USE)`` does not list rows it cannot then read.","     \"\"\"","-    workspa